# copy to .env (install.sh does this) — porthole loads it automatically; real env vars win
# A helper model powers the subagents and the context compressor: any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint.
# Leave HELPER_KEY and HELPER_URL empty to stay 100% local. (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY / DEEPSEEK_URL / DEEPSEEK_MODEL
# from older .env files are still accepted as fallbacks.)
#
# DeepSeek (the default: only the key is needed; a set HELPER_URL turns the helper on even without a key):
HELPER_KEY=
# HELPER_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# HELPER_MODEL=deepseek-flash
# OpenRouter:            HELPER_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1  HELPER_MODEL=<provider/model>  HELPER_KEY=sk-or-...
# Second local server:   HELPER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1  HELPER_MODEL=<model id>  (no key needed)
#
# Optional JSON object merged into every helper request, e.g. a provider's reasoning switch:
# HELPER_EXTRA_BODY={"reasoning": {"effort": "low"}}
